WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.613
Journey twenty-four: use Jubilee offline.

00:00:03.613 --> 00:00:08.311
New in this run: Jubilee opens with no connection, sends what was

00:00:08.311 --> 00:00:13.370
written even when it is closed, and leaves nothing behind at sign-out.

00:00:14.251 --> 00:00:18.095
The service worker keeps the app shell on the device.

00:00:18.095 --> 00:00:23.246
With the connection gone, the page loads again: Jubilee opens, with the

00:00:23.246 --> 00:00:27.235
directory saved at nine. Search waits for a connection.

00:00:28.124 --> 00:00:31.699
A conversation already opened is still readable.

00:00:31.699 --> 00:00:36.764
A message written now is kept on the device, marked Waiting to send.

00:00:39.048 --> 00:00:43.661
When the connection returns, it is sent with its idempotency key, and

00:00:43.661 --> 00:00:46.536
the banner says one saved message was sent.

00:00:47.582 --> 00:00:52.260
If Jubilee is closed by then, Background Sync wakes the service worker,

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.302
which sends the queue in order.

00:00:58.638 --> 00:01:01.681
On a slow connection, a warning says so.

00:01:01.681 --> 00:01:07.005
A save still sending is tried again, for up to a minute, until it goes

00:01:07.005 --> 00:01:07.614
through.

00:01:10.263 --> 00:01:15.028
Signing out removes the saved pages and any message still waiting, so

00:01:15.028 --> 00:01:17.583
nothing personal stays on the device.

00:01:18.638 --> 00:01:23.044
The tests also prove that the service worker never keeps an answer of

00:01:23.044 --> 00:01:27.578
the API, that nothing it sent is sent twice, and that a message waiting

00:01:27.578 --> 00:01:29.174
a day is marked Not sent.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:35.158
What is left is the owner's: the address of a status page for Check

00:01:35.158 --> 00:01:35.694
status.
